{"step_index":516,"source":"MODEL","type":"PLANNER_RESPONSE","status":"DONE","created_at":"2026-09-19T16:17:54Z","thinking":"The `analyze` function returned `None` for model 2 and model 3 because the data frames lacked any matching station metrics. Consequently, the analyses dictionary in the application's session state was populated with `None` values, leading to an incomplete analysis set. This incomplete or empty analyses caused downstream errors in chart generation and tab display.\n\n\nThe missing station metrics are due to the hardcoded column name lists in the utility module not including the column naming conventions used in Models 2 and 3. I will enhance the station metric resolver to dynamically discover station names by identifying columns containing \"Util\" or \"Utilization\", and subsequently pairing them with their corresponding queue time columns. This dynamic discovery is necessary to handle the varied naming conventions.\n\n\n","tool_calls":[{"name":"run_command","args":{"CommandLine":"python -c \"\nimport re\nimport pandas as pd\n\ndef smart_parse_stations(df):\n    row = df.mean(numeric_only=True).to_dict()\n    stations = {}\n    \n    # 1. Standard search\n    patterns = {\n        'Drilling': (['drilling util', 'drilling utilization', 'drill util'], ['drilling waiting time', 'drilling queue time', 'drill wait']),\n        'Milling': (['milling util', 'milling utilization', 'mill util'], ['milling waiting time', 'milling queue time', 'mill wait']),\n        'Assembly': (['assembly util', 'assembly utilization', 'asm util'], ['assembly waiting time', 'assembly queue time', 'asm wait', 'assembly time']),\n    }\n    \n    col_map_lower = {str(c).strip().lower(): c for c in df.columns}\n    \n    for st_name, (u_pats, w_pats) in patterns.items():\n        u_col = next((col_map_lower[p] for p in u_pats if p in col_map_lower), None)\n        w_col = next((col_map_lower[p] for p in w_pats if p in col_map_lower), None)\n        if u_col:\n            raw_u = row.get(u_col, 0.0)\n            u = raw_u / 100.0 if raw_u > 1.5 else raw_u\n            w = row.get(w_col, 0.0) if w_col else 0.0\n            stations[st_name] = {'utilization': round(float(u), 4), 'waiting_time': round(float(w), 2)}\n            \n    # If not found (e.g. Model 3), auto-discover\n    if not stations:\n        for c in df.columns:\n            clow = str(c).strip().lower()\n            if 'util' in clow:\n                st_name = re.sub(r'[_ ]*util(ization)?', '', str(c), flags=re.I).replace('_', ' ').strip()\n                if not st_name:\n                    st_name = str(c)\n                raw_u = row.get(c, 0.0)\n                u = raw_u / 100.0 if raw_u > 1.5 else raw_u\n                \n                # find queue or wait\n                base = re.sub(r'[_ ]*util(ization)?', '', str(c), flags=re.I).lower()\n                w_col = None\n                for candidate in df.columns:\n                    cand_low = str(candidate).strip().lower()\n                    if base in cand_low and ('queue' in cand_low or 'wait' in cand_low or 'time' in cand_low):\n                        w_col = candidate\n                        break\n                w = row.get(w_col, 0.0) if w_col else 0.0\n                stations[st_name] = {'utilization': round(float(u), 4), 'waiting_time': round(float(w), 2)}\n\n    return stations\n\nfor p in [r'D:\\acceleration\\Model_1.csv', r'D:\\acceleration\\Model_2.csv', r'D:\\acceleration\\Model_3.csv']:\n    df = pd.read_csv(p, nrows=2000)\n    st = smart_parse_stations(df)\n    bn = max(st.items(), key=lambda x: x[1]['utilization'])\n    print(p.split('\\\\\\\\')[-1], 'Found', len(st), 'stations. Bottleneck:', bn[0], f'{bn[1][\\\"utilization\\\"]*100:.1f}%')\n\"","Cwd":"C:\\Users\\win-10\\.gemini\\antigravity\\scratch\\neurax_app","IsDaemon":false,"WaitMsBeforeAsync":5000,"toolAction":"Testing smart station parser","toolSummary":"Test smart station parser"}}]}
